@scene chapter_2b_alchemists_scales

background: green_valley.jpg
music: wisdom_theme.mp3

dialogue:
"The path down from the Gate passes a crooked tower, leaning over the road like a curious neighbour."
"Every window leaks a different colour of smoke."
"A hand-painted sign reads: MEASUREMENTS TAKEN. TWICE. PROPERLY."

background: ancient_library.png

dialogue:
"Inside, the tower is all balances and bottles."
"Scales of every size hang from the rafters, each holding two small chests, each perfectly level."
"A wiry man peers at you over a pair of spectacles, then over a second pair on top of the first."

background: alchemist

npc Alchemist:
"Don't move. You'll disturb the readings."
"...There. You weigh about what I expected. Disappointing. I do so love a surprise."

npc You:
"Are you going to help me, or weigh me?"

npc Alchemist:
"Child, those are the same activity. Everything is measurement. Watch, and I'll prove it."

system skill_learned:
"MODULE UNLOCKED"
"THE ALCHEMIST'S SCALES"
"arithmetic · comparison · logic · precedence"

dialogue:
"— LESSON I — MIXING REAGENTS —"
"He tips two vials together. The System's numbers swirl in the glass."

npc Alchemist:
"To combine two numbers is to mix two reagents. You know plus and minus and times already."
"But three more earn their place on my shelf."
"Whole division that keeps only the whole — that is slash-slash. The leftovers — that is the percent sign. And raising a thing to a power — two stars."

interactive: scales_arithmetic

npc Alchemist:
"Good. Now mix three of them properly, on your own — a sum, a difference, a product. The System will check my scales against yours."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Combine two numbers into a sum, a difference, and a product."

mission: operators_intro

background: alchemist

npc Alchemist:
"Balanced to the grain. You have the hands of a measurer, whether you like it or not."

dialogue:
"— LESSON II — THE BALANCE —"
"He sets a great two-pan scale between you."

npc Alchemist:
"Now, the most misunderstood tool in this tower."
"A single equals sign POURS a value into a chest. You did that at your Awakening."
"But TWO equals signs do something entirely different. They WEIGH. They ask: are these two the same?"
"And the answer is never a number. It is always a truth — True, or False."

interactive: scales_weigh

npc Alchemist:
"Now build me a weighing. Not a pouring — a weighing. Mind the difference; it has bankrupted merchants."

interactive: scales_pour_vs_weigh

dialogue:
"— LESSON III — COMBINING WARDS —"
"He chalks three glowing wards onto the workbench."

npc Alchemist:
"Truths can be combined, as surely as reagents."
"AND demands both wards hold. OR is content with either. NOT flips a ward to its opposite."
"Learn their tempers."

interactive: scales_wards

npc Alchemist:
"Now sort these. Tell me at a glance which way each one tips."

interactive: scales_sort_true

dialogue:
"— LESSON IV — THE ORDER OF REAGENTS —"
"He holds up a warning finger, stained with a dozen colours."

npc Alchemist:
"One last law, and the deadliest. Reagents added in the wrong ORDER ruin the mixture."
"So it is with operators. Times comes before plus. Powers before either. And brackets — brackets go first of ALL."
"Guess wrong here and your potion explodes. Or worse: it quietly gives the wrong number, and you never notice."

interactive: scales_precedence

dialogue:
"— THE WARD THAT JUDGES —"
"He leads you to a sealed inner door, humming with a ward far older than the rest."

npc Alchemist:
"This ward judges every traveller. It opens only for one strong ENOUGH, and carrying the proper key."
"A weighing, and a ward, folded into a single verdict. Write it, and the door is yours."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Return True only if level is at least 5 AND has_key is True."

mission: alchemist_wards

background: ancient_library.png

dialogue:
"The ward reads your verdict, considers it, and clicks open onto a stair leading back down to the road."

npc Alchemist:
"Measured, weighed, and judged — all correct. Prove you hold the whole shelf, and I'll trouble you no further."

interactive: scales_final_recall

npc Alchemist:
"Arithmetic, a balance, and a ward, in one clean line. Off with you."
"You're bound for the chasm, I'd wager. Do give my regards to whatever's still broken down there."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Alchemist's Scales"
"Mastered: arithmetic · comparison (== vs =) · and / or / not · precedence"

reward:
xp: 75
gold: 40
achievement: MASTER OF THE SCALES

next:
chapter_3_endless_bridge
